{"id":"01a0657e-136f-72b8-a2fa-95727effdf66","chapterSlug":"rw7-02","paragraph":118,"wording":"[Guardswoman]","event":"named","holderQuote":"[Guardswoman] Leciss was gloating as she led Erin towards the large prison doors. Erin stared up apprehensively at the prison. The Dullahan was more sympathetic. He looked down at Erin as one of his arms held her shoulder. Separate from his body; the rest of him was walking a few feet to Erin’s right. His detached arm had hold of Erin. It was very creepy."}
{"id":"01a0657e-136f-758f-9b66-e0e911fa8fb3","chapterSlug":"rw7-02","paragraph":133,"wording":"[Guardswoman]","event":"named","holderQuote":"[Guardswoman] Leciss marched Erin into the prison. Now, they appeared closer to Liscor’s prison. Rows of cells, some with narrow steel bars, were the first thing Erin saw. She shuddered, but Pallass’ prison was far from dirty. In fact, it was uncannily clean and well-lit. Magical [Light] spells provided illumination and there wasn’t any smell of sewage or the bugs and stains that sprang to mind when Erin imagined a prison."}
{"id":"01a0657e-136f-741e-bbec-e1fd935ac3a1","chapterSlug":"rw7-02","paragraph":158,"wording":"[Guardswoman]","event":"named","holderQuote":"[Guardswoman] Leciss called over her shoulder. Left with that, Erin could only take stock of her surroundings."}
